/**
 * Food database — values are per 100 g (or per 100 ml for liquids).
 *
 * Sources: USDA FoodData Central, McCance & Widdowson (the UK/EU composition
 * tables) for European items, and IFCT (Indian Food Composition Tables) for
 * Indian ones. Trace minerals — biotin, iodine, chromium, molybdenum — are
 * sparsely reported everywhere, so those four columns are best-available
 * estimates and should be read as indicative rather than precise.
 *
 * ── CARBOHYDRATE CONVENTION — read this before adding data ──
 *
 * `carbs` INCLUDES fibre, which is the US/USDA convention.
 *
 * European labels do the opposite: under EU Regulation 1169/2011,
 * "carbohydrate" means *available* carbohydrate and fibre is declared
 * separately, so an EU label's number is smaller for the same food. Copying an
 * EU label straight into this file therefore understates carbs and breaks the
 * energy arithmetic — for rye crispbread that showed up as a 23% gap between
 * the stated calories and what the macros implied.
 *
 * To convert an EU label:  carbs = (label carbohydrate) + (label fibre)
 *
 * `scripts/audit-foods.mjs` catches this and runs on every build. It also
 * enforces that sugar and fibre never exceed carbs, sat fat never exceeds fat,
 * and that no plant food claims cholesterol or unfortified B12.
 *
 * diet tag:  'vegan' | 'vegetarian' (lacto) | 'egg' | 'nonveg'
 */

