  /* ================================ BREAD ================================
     Values follow McCance & Widdowson (UK/EU composition tables) rather than
     USDA, because European bread differs materially: less added sugar, and
     UK/EU salt-reduction targets have pushed sodium well below typical US
     loaves. Fortification also differs — UK white and brown flour is required
     by law to carry calcium, iron, thiamin and niacin, which is why white
     bread here is not the nutritional blank it is often assumed to be.

     "Brown" and "wholemeal" are not the same thing and the difference is the
     usual reason people think they are eating more fibre than they are: brown
     is roughly 85% extraction, wholemeal is 100% and has about half as much
     fibre again. */
